                        1284 --1374:  *    #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0STC, #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPA, #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPB, <br>
                        1285 --1375:  *    #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPC, #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPS, #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPT, (Used by sub functions)
                        1286 --1376:  *    #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0DPW
                        1287 --1377:  * \par Precondition
                        1288 --1378:  *  - The RSA Context value must have been set beforehand.
                        1289 --1379:  * \par Detailed description
                        1290 --1380:  *      - Calculate m used in CRT mode.
                        1291 --1381:  *      - When calling with #PKCD_RSA_CRT_OPERATE_NOT_CALLED == p_prm->operate_call_cnt, calculate m1 and <br>
                        1292 --1382:  *        when calling with #PKCD_RSA_CRT_OPERATE_CALLED_ONCE == p_prm->operate_call_cnt, calculate m2.
                        1293 --1383:  *        when calling with #PKCD_RSA_CRT_OPERATE_CALLED_TWICE == p_prm->operate_call_cnt, #PKCD_RET_INTERNALERR <br>
                        1294 --1384:  *        returned.
                        1295 --1385:  * \par Remarks
                        1296 --1386:  *  - None
                        1297 --1387:  *
                        1298 --1388:  * Pseudo-code for the function can be found below.
                        1299 --1389:  * -# Initialize the variable ret with #PKCD_RET_INTERNALERR.
                        1300 --1390:  * -# If #PKCD_RSA_CRT_OPERATE_NOT_CALLED == p_prm->operate_call_cnt then
                        1301 --1391:  *   -# If #PKC_BOOL_FALSE != p_ctx->sec_mod_exp, then
                        1302 --1392:  *     -# Calculate m1 with the #r_pkcd_rsa_calc_m_sec.
                        1303 --1393:  *   -# Else
                        1304 --1394:  *     -# Calculate m1 with the #r_pkcd_rsa_calc_m.
