                        1712 --1831:  * \par Precondition
                        1713 --1832:  *  - None
                        1714 --1833:  * \par Detailed description
                        1715 --1834:  *      - Calculate the GCD(greatest common divisor) of x and y.
                        1716 --1835:  *      - The algorithm is described in chapter 14.61 of HANDBOOK of APPLIED CRYPTOGRAPHY.
                        1717 --1836:  *      - Since it is necessary for the #r_pkcd_rsa_inverse, it outputs D together with GCD v.
                        1718 --1837:  *      - The signs of A,B,C and D are managed separately from the value.
                        1719 --1838:  * \par Remarks
                        1720 --1839:  *  - None
                        1721 --1840:  *
                        1722 --1841:  * Pseudo-code for the function can be found below.
                        1723 --1842:  * -# Initialize the variable ret with #PKCD_RET_INTERNALERR.
                        1724 --1843:  * -# Set the larger of xlen and ylen to len.
                        1725 --1844:  * -# Add 8 bytes to len_u 32 in consideration of carry.
                        1726 --1845:  * -# Set data lengt to DL bit of #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0OMR with the #r_pkcd_cmn_set_dl
                        1727 --1846:  * -# Set 1 in PKCC format to p_pkccram_one.
                        1728 --1847:  * -# Copy x in work area of u with the #r_pkcd_cmn_cpy_by_64bounds
                        1729 --1848:  * -# Copy y in work area of v with the #r_pkcd_cmn_cpy_by_64bounds
                        1730 --1849:  * -# Set 0 to B and C work area.
                        1731 --1850:  * -# Set 1 to A and D work area.
                        1732 --1851:  * -# Clear sign flag.
                        1733 --1852:  * -# Set 0 to div2_cnt.
