                        2326 --2505:  *
                        2327 --2506:  * Pseudo-code for the function can be found below.
                        2328 --2507:  * -# Initialize the variable ret with #PKCD_RET_INTERNALERR.
                        2329 --2508:  * -# Set dlen to DL bit of #PKCD_CMN_ICUM_PKCCB0OMR with the #r_pkcd_cmn_set_dl
                        2330 --2509:  * -# Set WORK to ICUM_PKCCB0DPX
                        2331 --2510:  * -# Set Prime number d to #PKCD_RSA_WORK1
                        2332 --2511:  * -# Get the least significant byte of d.
                        2333 --2512:  * -# If LSB is not 0 then
                        2334 --2513:  *   -# Loop while i is #PKCD_RSA_PRIME_TBL_SIZE or less increment i for each loop
                        2335 --2514:  *     -# Copy divisor in #g_rsa_prime_table to WORK area.
                        2336 --2515:  *     -# Copy Montgomery Reduction in #g_rsa_mont_reduction_table to WORK area.
                        2337 --2516:  *     -# Calculate dR^(-1) mod divisor with mode #PKCD_CMN_MODE_ARINVMODC of #r_pkcd_cmn_run.
                        2338 --2517:  *     -# Check the remainder and set ret to #PKCD_RET_RSA_COMPOSITE if it is 0
